WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.162
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:15.432 --> 00:18.060
Sorry. Just a little longer.

3
00:20.820 --> 00:25.891
What does the after-party organizer for a wedding actually do?

4
00:26.735 --> 00:30.030
Booking the venue, planning the schedule, stuff like that.

5
00:30.030 --> 00:32.370
We can't make invitations until we pick a place.

6
00:32.370 --> 00:35.090
And we need a video.

7
00:35.090 --> 00:38.260
It's not like you're that close with Moriya.

8
00:38.260 --> 00:41.100
You didn't have to take on something so complicated.

9
00:41.100 --> 00:44.500
Well, I've organized after-parties a few times before.

10
00:44.500 --> 00:48.410
They said they'll let us take care of everything.

11
00:49.020 --> 00:50.540
Us?

12
00:59.601 --> 01:02.419
Look at my phone anytime.

13
01:02.419 --> 01:03.380
What?

14
01:03.380 --> 01:07.550
The code is my employee number, 17135.

15
01:07.550 --> 01:09.400
What's this all of a sudden?

16
01:09.400 --> 01:12.840
I'm coordinating with the bride's organizer,

17
01:12.840 --> 01:16.170
so I might check my phone or take calls while I'm with you.

18
01:16.170 --> 01:20.600
I might be alone with her looking at places too, but don't worry.

19
01:20.600 --> 01:22.190
I'm not worried.

20
01:22.190 --> 01:24.340
Huh? Be worried.

21
01:26.837 --> 01:29.640
I'm kinda joking, but still...

22
01:29.640 --> 01:33.910
It'd make me feel better if you look freely, okay?

23
01:35.920 --> 01:37.630
Really?

24
01:50.660 --> 01:52.350
Weird dog...

25
01:56.970 --> 01:59.280
You made this your pic?

26
01:59.280 --> 02:00.520
Yeah.

27
02:01.640 --> 02:04.490
Read the start of the chat.

28
02:04.490 --> 02:07.370
[Hi, it's Mitsuki! Is that picture a sumo thing?]

29
02:07.370 --> 02:09.230
Sumo? Really?

30
02:09.230 --> 02:10.340
Right?

31
02:10.340 --> 02:12.830
I didn't know sumo wrestlers used something similar.

32
02:12.830 --> 02:15.620
How old is she? Is she just naturally like this?

33
02:15.620 --> 02:19.164
Same age as us, and normal. A proper kind of person.

34
02:21.890 --> 02:23.210
Thanks.

35
02:23.870 --> 02:25.280
You're done?

36
02:25.280 --> 02:27.630
Because nothing looks suspicious.

37
02:27.630 --> 02:31.400
I mean, you could easily hide whatever you don't want to show anyway.

38
02:31.400 --> 02:33.390
Then look at everything else too.

39
02:33.390 --> 02:35.290
Jeez, it's fine.

40
02:35.290 --> 02:37.570
Why do you want me to distrust you?

41
02:39.050 --> 02:40.750
It's not like that.

42
03:05.936 --> 03:10.176
It started with an email.

43
03:11.610 --> 03:15.890
[No Subject] [Sorry for the late-night message.]

44
03:17.948 --> 03:19.608
That's exactly why...

45
03:46.100 --> 03:50.508
[Mitsuki: Does your company use a slow juicer that you would recommend?]

46
04:58.859 --> 05:02.497
[Recommended Users]

47
05:06.640 --> 05:08.230
Weird dog...

48
05:16.810 --> 05:19.510
[Mi]

49
05:25.400 --> 05:27.710
Nakarai.

50
05:27.710 --> 05:33.120
IT just said it's about time you change your computer password.

51
05:34.460 --> 05:37.770
They said you can't log in once it expires.

52
05:38.710 --> 05:41.660
Right. Thanks.

53
06:09.820 --> 06:13.264
[This password is already in use.]

54
06:25.240 --> 06:28.840
This Saturday, I'm going a bit far out of town.

55
06:28.840 --> 06:30.820
- For the after-party? - Yeah.

56
06:30.820 --> 06:33.080
The bride's grandpa lives in Gunma,

57
06:33.080 --> 06:35.520
so we're filming him as a surprise.

58
06:35.520 --> 06:39.200
He doesn't know how to take videos on his phone.

59
06:39.860 --> 06:41.890
You're going with the girl?

60
06:42.710 --> 06:45.451
Yes. By rental car.

61
06:47.657 --> 06:49.730
That's a lot of work.

62
07:14.749 --> 07:19.053
[Wedding After-Party]

63
08:23.920 --> 08:26.130
[Mitsuki: How does this look?]

64
08:26.130 --> 08:28.880
[Wow, this looks amazing! Thank you!]

65
08:28.880 --> 08:31.250
[Glad I could help!]

66
08:43.180 --> 08:45.270
[Oh, gosh. He's totally my type.]

67
08:45.270 --> 08:48.060
[It wasn't a sumo tag. I bet I seem so dumb.]

68
08:48.060 --> 08:51.480
[I wonder who he went to the festival with. Was it a girl?]

69
08:51.480 --> 08:54.560
[It feels so nice being helpful.]

70
08:54.560 --> 08:58.478
[He said it looks great! I'm gonna be happy for days.]

71
09:03.584 --> 09:06.209
Wait, where did I put my wallet?

72
09:06.209 --> 09:08.480
- Table for three. - Right. This way, please.

73
09:09.750 --> 09:11.450
Oh, excuse me.

74
09:13.350 --> 09:14.640
Sorry,

75
09:14.640 --> 09:17.440
I need to go check out a venue tonight for the after-party,

76
09:17.440 --> 09:19.360
so I can't come over tonight anymore.

77
09:19.360 --> 09:20.960
Sure, okay.

78
09:20.960 --> 09:22.760
I'll be in touch.

79
09:31.390 --> 09:33.830
Are you alone today?

80
09:33.830 --> 09:35.520
I am.

81
09:36.120 --> 09:37.130
The other day...

82
09:37.130 --> 09:39.690
Ayuko, come switch with me for a sec.

83
09:41.160 --> 09:42.610
Okay.

84
09:47.920 --> 09:51.590
[Mocchi showed me his ex's photo. She's a beauty... I'm so depressed.]

85
09:51.590 --> 09:54.093
You dated for a long time, right?

86
09:54.093 --> 09:55.434
I guess so.

87
09:55.434 --> 09:58.134
Why did you break up with her?

88
09:59.224 --> 10:01.894
Well, a lot happened.

89
10:03.390 --> 10:05.000
A lot...

90
10:08.960 --> 10:12.990
Sorry, I overstepped just now.

91
10:12.990 --> 10:14.890
No, it's totally fine.

92
10:29.600 --> 10:31.450
I'll be back by night.

93
10:33.280 --> 10:34.640
Okay.

94
10:34.640 --> 10:37.020
Drive safe.

95
10:37.020 --> 10:39.350
Yes. I'll drive carefully.

96
10:39.350 --> 10:41.540
- See you. - Okay.

97
10:49.140 --> 10:52.240
I wanted to make lunch for tomorrow's trip,

98
10:52.240 --> 10:56.860
but he said he'd find a tasty restaurant for us nearby.

99
10:56.860 --> 11:00.100
That's kind of him, but ruthless too.

100
11:03.540 --> 11:06.271
But I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

101
11:06.271 --> 11:09.167
What is wrong with me?

102
11:10.030 --> 11:14.020
Will he notice I got new nails?

103
11:14.800 --> 11:19.110
I wonder what kind of fashion he likes.

104
11:22.630 --> 11:24.300
Welcome.

105
11:40.800 --> 11:45.920
And he's so cool, with long fingers.

106
11:45.920 --> 11:47.440
His fingers too.

107
11:50.390 --> 11:53.197
A girl on this earth gets to

108
11:53.197 --> 11:56.700
intertwine her fingers with those fingers of his.

109
11:56.700 --> 11:59.290
This color seems like you, Nakarai.

110
12:06.079 --> 12:10.729
I know there's nothing between us. But still...

111
12:18.572 --> 12:20.036
That's tasty.

112
12:24.720 --> 12:29.450
I want to stare at the side of his handsome face forever.

113
12:38.091 --> 12:39.959
Sorry.

114
12:39.959 --> 12:41.529
Come on.

115
12:54.690 --> 12:55.750
Hello?

116
12:55.750 --> 12:58.310
Nakarai! Help me!

117
12:58.310 --> 12:59.500
Huh?

118
13:09.170 --> 13:11.165
Sorry, Nakarai.

119
13:11.165 --> 13:13.130
No one else would pick up.

120
13:13.130 --> 13:15.850
It's okay. I've done it too.

121
13:20.020 --> 13:22.830
Working on a day off is rough.

122
13:29.700 --> 13:31.720
I'm not working.

123
13:32.920 --> 13:35.340
I didn't want to be at home.

124
13:36.030 --> 13:37.590
Is something wrong?

125
13:38.400 --> 13:40.520
Will you hear me out?

126
13:40.520 --> 13:41.810
Sure.

127
13:43.220 --> 13:47.740
There's this idol I Stan,

128
13:48.410 --> 13:50.940
and a dating scandal came out yesterday.

129
13:52.380 --> 13:55.234
So when I was alone at home agonizing over it,

130
13:55.234 --> 13:57.060
I couldn't take it.

131
13:57.740 --> 14:00.630
So I ran away to the office.

132
14:01.310 --> 14:03.250
I see.

133
14:04.927 --> 14:08.140
I might not be able to support him anymore...

134
14:08.830 --> 14:12.250
But I guess that can't be helped.

135
14:14.870 --> 14:16.240
All right.

136
14:16.240 --> 14:18.930
I'm gonna do Pilates five days a week.

137
14:18.930 --> 14:19.860
Huh?

138
14:19.860 --> 14:24.240
I wanna channel these feelings into something positive, you know?

139
14:24.240 --> 14:28.400
It's not like I can tell him how I feel in person.

140
14:30.162 --> 14:34.492
And I don't want to regret falling for him.

141
14:37.430 --> 14:38.440
Oh, right.

142
14:38.440 --> 14:41.990
I'll give you a proper thank-you later, but here.

143
14:41.990 --> 14:44.400
- What's this? - It was a gift.

144
14:44.400 --> 14:46.830
Apparently it tastes good soaked in whiskey.

145
14:57.530 --> 14:59.660
I'm home.

146
14:59.660 --> 15:01.390
Sorry I'm late.

147
15:01.390 --> 15:03.470
Traffic was bad.

148
15:05.754 --> 15:07.294
Nakarai?

149
15:09.050 --> 15:12.361
Sorry, were you waiting up for me?

150
15:14.350 --> 15:16.740
Huh? Are you drunk?

151
15:18.168 --> 15:20.210
What's that?

152
15:20.210 --> 15:22.170
Gummies.

153
15:22.170 --> 15:24.440
Those aren't just gummies.

154
15:25.920 --> 15:28.540
They reek of alcohol.

155
15:30.010 --> 15:31.950
While I was waiting at home,

156
15:31.950 --> 15:36.010
I wanted something to snack on, and I couldn't stop.

157
15:37.500 --> 15:39.680
You wanted something to snack on?

158
15:42.210 --> 15:46.250
Hagiwara, don't you have something to say?

159
15:46.250 --> 15:47.250
Huh?

160
15:47.250 --> 15:49.790
Anything you wanna tell me?

161
15:49.790 --> 15:51.530
Huh?

162
15:51.530 --> 15:53.170
No, not really...

163
15:53.170 --> 15:54.540
Liar.

164
15:54.540 --> 15:56.350
What?

165
15:56.350 --> 15:58.110
There isn't. Really.

166
15:58.110 --> 16:00.270
Think harder.

167
16:00.270 --> 16:01.790
Huh?

168
16:04.060 --> 16:05.790
There's nothing to say.

169
16:05.790 --> 16:08.890
No guilty secrets. Cheating is out of the question.

170
16:08.890 --> 16:11.080
And no group dates either.

171
16:17.270 --> 16:19.800
I have something to say to you.

172
16:19.800 --> 16:22.030
Huh? You do?

173
16:22.030 --> 16:24.890
What? You're scaring me.

174
16:27.360 --> 16:31.590
I looked at your phone, Hagiwara.

175
16:32.220 --> 16:34.970
The one where you're messaging that girl.

176
16:35.660 --> 16:37.020
Sorry.

177
16:38.410 --> 16:40.640
What? That's all?

178
16:40.640 --> 16:43.530
I said you could look. It's totally fine.

179
16:43.530 --> 16:45.270
That's not all.

180
16:46.060 --> 16:50.410
I found her social media account and looked at it.

181
16:51.470 --> 16:53.610
Seriously?

182
16:53.610 --> 16:56.960
Well, I haven't done anything I'd need to keep secret.

183
16:59.260 --> 17:01.800
I was like, "Dammit".

184
17:01.800 --> 17:03.090
Huh?

185
17:04.120 --> 17:06.870
The way that girl sees you, Hagiwara,

186
17:06.870 --> 17:09.550
is as a capable, organized guy.

187
17:09.550 --> 17:12.550
Kind and polite,

188
17:13.210 --> 17:15.210
with beautiful fingers.

189
17:15.210 --> 17:17.020
Thank you?

190
17:17.650 --> 17:22.750
But even after falling for you, you didn't give her any openings.

191
17:23.720 --> 17:27.100
Yet every little thing you did would excite her.

192
17:29.740 --> 17:33.950
We didn't have that kind of thing.

193
17:35.240 --> 17:41.310
Even before we thought about love, we got close and had sex.

194
17:44.000 --> 17:45.510
True.

195
17:48.610 --> 17:54.630
The things we skipped over were there on her social media.

196
18:04.890 --> 18:06.690
So, I...

197
18:08.960 --> 18:13.890
fell for you again through her eyes.

198
18:17.810 --> 18:21.170
So, after I fell in love, I fell in love again.

199
18:24.897 --> 18:26.758
Darn it.

200
18:28.560 --> 18:32.090
Hey, stop that.

201
18:36.440 --> 18:38.400
Anything else to say?

202
18:40.400 --> 18:43.400
I was jealous that you went out together too.

203
18:46.420 --> 18:48.910
Let's go out when things settle down.

204
19:08.790 --> 19:09.900
Let's eat gummies.

205
19:09.900 --> 19:10.990
You look sleepy.

206
19:10.990 --> 19:12.640
- Gummies! - Huh?

207
19:21.940 --> 19:24.700
[Oh, gosh. Just seeing her in her dress made me cry.]

208
19:24.700 --> 19:28.068
[He left in a hurry. I can tell he has someone he likes.]

209
19:35.030 --> 19:36.620
Nakarai!

210
19:45.500 --> 19:47.370
Why are you laughing?

211
19:47.370 --> 19:48.830
It's nothing.

212
19:49.880 --> 19:51.821
You're finally back.

213
20:04.010 --> 20:07.290
By the way, what happened the other night?

214
20:07.290 --> 20:10.330
The "anything wanna tell me?" thing.

215
20:10.330 --> 20:11.877
What's that?

216
20:11.877 --> 20:13.770
Did I say that?

217
20:13.770 --> 20:16.210
Huh? You don't remember?

218
20:16.210 --> 20:18.910
You pressed me really hard.

219
20:18.910 --> 20:22.750
You kept asking, "Don't you have something to say to me?"

220
20:23.550 --> 20:25.190
Don't brush this off!

221
20:25.190 --> 20:27.590
So, what was that about?

222
20:27.590 --> 20:29.210
I had no idea what you meant.

223
20:29.210 --> 20:31.760
I thought so much, I couldn't sleep.

224
20:33.540 --> 20:35.400
Oh, I remember.

225
20:35.400 --> 20:36.580
What?

226
20:36.580 --> 20:38.570
The password.

227
20:38.570 --> 20:39.720
Huh?

228
20:39.720 --> 20:41.700
The company login password.

229
20:41.700 --> 20:44.270
You used my name, didn't you?

230
20:46.538 --> 20:49.410
Oh, that?

231
20:49.410 --> 20:51.170
When I tried to use it,

232
20:51.170 --> 20:54.370
it said, "This password is already in use".

233
20:55.710 --> 20:57.640
It might not be me though.

234
20:57.640 --> 21:00.970
For example, maybe someone has a crush on you.

235
21:00.970 --> 21:02.980
But it was you, right?

236
21:04.280 --> 21:05.770
You caught me.

237
21:06.930 --> 21:10.210
Is it fun using my name and birthday?

238
21:10.210 --> 21:11.460
Password thief.

239
21:11.460 --> 21:15.310
Because every time I enter my password, I think of you, Nakarai.

240
21:15.310 --> 21:16.930
Nice, right?

241
21:21.360 --> 21:23.200
If you do that,

242
21:23.200 --> 21:27.220
I'll run out of words I can use for my passwords.

243
21:27.220 --> 21:30.840
Let's not use each other's info in our passwords.

244
21:30.840 --> 21:32.400
What?

245
21:33.000 --> 21:36.090
A mutual non-aggression pact.

246
21:36.090 --> 21:37.620
Okay.

247
21:40.820 --> 21:42.301
A wedding favor?

248
21:42.301 --> 21:45.806
Yeah. I got one... Huh? Wait, what?

249
21:48.058 --> 21:50.468
Oh, I see.

250
21:52.020 --> 21:54.020
It's raining again, huh?

251
21:54.020 --> 21:55.680
It's not me.

252
21:56.984 --> 21:58.954
This rain's pretty heavy.

253
22:00.570 --> 22:01.810
I'm home.

254
22:01.810 --> 22:03.230
I'm home.

255
22:04.120 --> 22:05.780
What was the wedding favor?

256
22:05.780 --> 22:07.900
Just wait a second.

257
22:24.250 --> 22:27.988
[Thank you] [Vostok]

258
22:31.101 --> 22:34.325
[Vostok Designer] [Kazuaki Fujisawa]

259
22:35.910 --> 22:37.790
What is it?

260
22:37.790 --> 22:39.140
Glasses.

261
22:40.850 --> 22:41.945
Can I see?

262
22:41.945 --> 22:43.195
Go ahead.

263
22:53.940 --> 22:57.800
They're tilting, but like they're leaning on each other.

264
22:58.560 --> 22:59.910
Yeah.

265
23:08.549 --> 23:10.239
They're well-made.

266
23:15.200 --> 23:17.070
Shall we toast?

267
23:17.070 --> 23:18.750
To what?

268
23:18.750 --> 23:21.720
To an ordinary day, I guess.

269
23:22.470 --> 23:24.060
Oh, jeez.

270
23:33.410 --> 23:36.310
A toast to an ordinary day. Cheers.

271
23:36.310 --> 23:37.780
Cheers.

272
23:45.610 --> 23:48.060
- A girl from a normal family, huh? - In this day and age?

273
23:48.060 --> 23:49.970
Be nice to your parents when they're alive.

274
23:49.970 --> 23:52.598
What could I possibly do or say in response to that?

275
23:52.598 --> 23:55.700
That just means everyone wants what's best for other people.

276
23:55.700 --> 23:57.600
Ask more. "Is it mine?"

277
23:57.600 --> 23:59.010
Is it mine?
